@acepace Well, this is 100% usable as is, because the patched version of TypeORM is used at our production for like 6 months already.

However, I haven't dived too much into TypeORM's internals because we've in the middle of migrating to MikroORM and most probably @nebkat 's comments should be taken into account before merging this into the mainline. 

I think I will finish with this until the end of the week, but another question is – how time much will it take to merge it after changes I'll make.

If you need to use it right now I suggest you to:
1) Install the latest version of TypeORM (or update an existing one) and commit changes; 
2) Clone my branch containing the fix;
3) Build it manually;
4) Put the build result files into corresponding typeorm directory at your project's node_modules
5) Use patch-package to make a permanent patch

